= Arbitrage — Technical =

A textbook arbitrage portfolio has initial value V_0≤0 and terminal payoff V_T≥0 almost surely with P(V_T>0)>0. DeFi arbitrage is typically not frictionless: gas, fees, transaction ordering, state changes, failed execution, and inventory constraints alter the opportunity.

== Modeling / security cautions ==
* arbitrage ≠ ordinary speculation
* arbitrage opportunity ≠ guaranteed executable profit
* arbitrage pressure ≠ perfect price equality

== References ==
* Stephen A. Ross, “The Arbitrage Theory of Capital Asset Pricing” (1976), for no-arbitrage foundations.
* Andrei Shleifer & Robert Vishny, “The Limits of Arbitrage” (1997).
* BIS, “Trading in the DeFi era: automated market-maker” (2021), for AMM arbitrage mechanics.
